{"title": "Sectional Mock #72 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A boat covers 56 km downstream in 4 hours and 28 km upstream in 7 hours. What is its speed in still water (in kmph)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 56 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 28 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8", "10", "9", "12"], "options_hi": ["8", "10", "9", "12"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let, speed of boat in still water and speed of stream be b km/h and s km/h respectively.</p><p>Downstream speed = 56/4 = 14 km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 28/7 = 4 km/h</p><p>b + s = 14, b  -  s = 4 =&gt; 2b = 18 =&gt; b = 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, speed of boat in still water and speed of stream be b km/h and s km/h respectively.</p><p>Downstream speed = 56/4 = 14 km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 28/7 = 4 km/h</p><p>b + s = 14, b  -  s = 4 =&gt; 2b = 18 =&gt; b = 9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average of the smallest composite number that is less than 90 and the largest prime number that is less than 105 is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>90 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 105 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["95.5", "71.5", "69.5", "53.5"], "options_hi": ["95.5", "71.5", "69.5", "53.5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The smallest composite number that is less than 90 = 4</p><p>The largest prime number that is less than 105 = 103</p><p>Hence, the required average = (103 + 4)/2 = 53.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The smallest composite number that is less than 90 = 4</p><p>The largest prime number that is less than 105 = 103</p><p>Hence, the required average = (103 + 4)/2 = 53.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The age of Atul, Vibha and Karan are in AP respectively. After two years, the age of Atul is one-third of the age of Karan and present age of Vibha is 3 years less than thrice of the present age of Atul. Find the sum of their current ages.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354;, &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2309;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["30 years", "24 years", "36 years", "42 years"], "options_hi": ["30 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "24 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354;", "36 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "42 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the age of Atul, Vibha and Karan are (a  -  d), a and (a + d) respectively.</p><p>Now,</p><p>(a  -  d) + 2 = 1/3 * (a + d + 2)</p><p>a = 2d  -  2 -----(1)</p><p>and</p><p>a = 3 * (a  -  d)  -  3</p><p>2a = 3d + 3 -----(2)</p><p>From eqn (1) and (2)  -  </p><p>4d  -  4 = 3d + 3</p><p>d = 7, a = 12</p><p>Sum of their current ages = a  -  d + a + a + d = 3*12 = 36 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the age of Atul, Vibha and Karan are (a  -  d), a and (a + d) respectively.</p><p>Now,</p><p>(a  -  d) + 2 = 1/3 * (a + d + 2)</p><p>a = 2d  -  2 -----(1)</p><p>and</p><p>a = 3 * (a  -  d)  -  3</p><p>2a = 3d + 3 -----(2)</p><p>From eqn (1) and (2)  -  </p><p>4d  -  4 = 3d + 3</p><p>d = 7, a = 12</p><p>Sum of their current ages = a  -  d + a + a + d = 3*12 = 36 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a = sin &#952; + cos &#952;, then find the value of:</p><p><div>&nbsp;[cos &theta;(1 + tan &theta;)]<sup>2</sup> - 5[ cos &theta; (1 + tan &theta; -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin &theta;", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a = sin &#952; + cos &#952; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379;</p><p> <div>&nbsp;[cos &theta;(1 + tan &theta;)]<sup>2</sup> - 5[ cos &theta; (1 + tan &theta; -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin &theta;", "options_en": ["a<sup>2</sup>  -  5a", "a<sup>2</sup> + 5", "5a<sup>2</sup> + a", "a<sup>2</sup>  -  a"], "options_hi": ["a<sup>2</sup> - 5a", "a<sup>2</sup> + 5", "5a<sup>2</sup> + a", "a<sup>2</sup> - a"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=463 height=173 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11734/image019.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=463 height=173 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11734/image019.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Aman invested a sum of money in scheme A at the rate of 8% p.a. for a period of 5 years on simple interest. He invested four times of the sum of scheme A in scheme B at the rate of 5% p.a. for 7 years on simple interest. He received a total interest amount of &#8377;1,620. How much (in &#8377;) did he invest in scheme B?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2309;&#2350;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2350; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 8% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2350; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2350; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 5% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 1,620 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2350; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["2,400", "900", "3,200", "3,600"], "options_hi": ["2,400", "900", "3,200", "3,600"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>In scheme A,</p><p>Let amount invested be x,</p><p>Rate=8%,</p><p>Time=5 years</p><p>So S.I=x*8*5/100</p><p>In scheme B,</p><p>Amount invested=4x,</p><p>Rate=5%</p><p>Time=7 years</p><p>S.I=4x*5*7/100</p><p>Total= scheme A+scheme B,So</p><p>40x/100 + 140x/100=1620</p><p>180x=162000</p><p>X=900.</p><p>So 4x=3600.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In scheme A,</p><p>Let amount invested be x,</p><p>Rate=8%,</p><p>Time=5 years</p><p>So S.I=x*8*5/100</p><p>In scheme B,</p><p>Amount invested=4x,</p><p>Rate=5%</p><p>Time=7 years</p><p>S.I=4x*5*7/100</p><p>Total= scheme A+scheme B,So</p><p>40x/100 + 140x/100=1620</p><p>180x=162000</p><p>X=900.</p><p>So 4x=3600.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number of heads on the farm, as determined by the farmer, was 60. When he counted, he discovered there were 150 legs. If all that was present were pigeons or horses, and every horse on the property had four legs while every pigeon had two, how many horses were there on the property?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2326;&#2375;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 60 &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; 150 &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2348;&#2370;&#2340;&#2352; &#2351;&#2366; &#2328;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2328;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2348;&#2370;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2341;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["14", "12", "15", "10"], "options_hi": ["14", "12", "15", "10"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let h = number of horses, p = number of pigeons</p><p>h + p = 60 (heads)</p><p>4h + 2p = 150 (legs)</p><p>Simplify legs: 2h + p = 75</p><p>Subtract heads equation: (2h + p) - (h + p) = 75 - 60</p><p>h = <b>15</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let h = number of horses, p = number of pigeons</p><p>h + p = 60 (heads)</p><p>4h + 2p = 150 (legs)</p><p>Simplify legs: 2h + p = 75</p><p>Subtract heads equation: (2h + p) - (h + p) = 75 - 60</p><p>h = <b>15</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cylindrical tank of diameter 21cm is partially filled with water. If a cubical metal block of side 14cm is immersed into it, the water level in the tank will rise approximately by how much level?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2310;&#2306;&#2358;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2381;&#2354;&#2377;&#2325; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2369;&#2348;&#2379;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["7.426 cm", "7.526 cm", "7.922 cm", "8.526 cm"], "options_hi": ["7.426 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "7.526 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "7.922 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "8.526 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the cubical block = 14<sup>3</sup> = 2744</p><p>Volume of the water raised/ volume of the cubical block = &#960; * 10.5<sup>2</sup> * raised water level</p><p>Raised water level = 2744 / &#960; * 10.5<sup>2</sup> = 7.922 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the cubical block = 14<sup>3</sup> = 2744</p><p>Volume of the water raised/ volume of the cubical block = &#960; * 10.5<sup>2</sup> * raised water level</p><p>Raised water level = 2744 / &#960; * 10.5<sup>2</sup> = 7.922 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A school sports teacher purchases 7 badminton rackets and 6 shuttlecocks for &#8377;7600. Later, she buys 3 badminton rackets and 5 shuttlecocks for &#8377;3500. Find the cost of each racket and each shuttlecock respectively.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2360; &#2335;&#2368;&#2330;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 7 &#2348;&#2376;&#2337;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335;&#2344; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; 7600 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 3 &#2348;&#2376;&#2337;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335;&#2344; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; 3500 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.500 and Rs.50", "Rs.1000 and Rs.100", "Rs.500 and Rs.100", "Rs.1000 and Rs.150"], "options_hi": ["500 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2352;&#2369;.", "1000 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2352;&#2369;.", "500 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2352;&#2369;.", "1000 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 150 &#2352;&#2369;."], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let price of each racket and each shuttlecock be Rs. A, and Rs. B respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>7A + 6B = 7600 ... (1)</p><p>3A + 5B = 3500 ... (2)</p><p>After solving equation (1) and (2).</p><p>B = 100 and A = 1000</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>Cost of each racket = Rs.1000</p><p>And cost of each shuttlecock = Rs.100</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let price of each racket and each shuttlecock be Rs. A, and Rs. B respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>7A + 6B = 7600 ... (1)</p><p>3A + 5B = 3500 ... (2)</p><p>After solving equation (1) and (2).</p><p>B = 100 and A = 1000</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>Cost of each racket = Rs.1000</p><p>And cost of each shuttlecock = Rs.100</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Solve (X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup>/X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>) * (X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>/X<sup>-5</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-4</sup>Y<sup>-1</sup>/X<sup>2</sup> Y<sup>2</sup>) = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup>/X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>) * (X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>/X<sup>-5</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-4</sup>Y<sup>-1</sup>/X<sup>2</sup> Y<sup>2</sup>) = ?, &#2361;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; ?</p>", "options_en": ["X<sup>13</sup> Y<sup>-4</sup>", "X<sup>13</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>", "X<sup>-13</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>", "X<sup>13</sup> Y<sup>4</sup>"], "options_hi": ["X<sup>13</sup> Y<sup>-4</sup>", "X<sup>13</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>", "X<sup>-13</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>", "X<sup>13</sup> Y<sup>4</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>(X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup>/X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>)  * (X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>/X<sup>-5</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-4</sup>Y<sup>-1</sup>/X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>) = (X<sup>-1</sup>Y<sup>-7</sup>) )  * (X<sup>8</sup>Y<sup>0</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-6</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>)</p><p>= (X<sup>7</sup>Y<sup>-7</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-6</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>) = X<sup>13</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup>/X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>3</sup>)  * (X<sup>3</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>/X<sup>-5</sup>Y<sup>-2</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-4</sup>Y<sup>-1</sup>/X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup>) = (X<sup>-1</sup>Y<sup>-7</sup>) )  * (X<sup>8</sup>Y<sup>0</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-6</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>)</p><p>= (X<sup>7</sup>Y<sup>-7</sup>) &div; (X<sup>-6</sup>Y<sup>-3</sup>) = X<sup>13</sup>Y<sup>-4</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The line graph shows the production (in tonnes) and the sales (in tonnes) of a company.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image035.png\"></p><p>What percentage (approximately) of the total production of the company is the total sales of the company in all the years together? (correct upto 2 decimal places)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; (&#2335;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2335;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image035.png\"></p><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;, &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; (&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)</p>", "options_en": ["78.44", "68.12", "72.55", "75"], "options_hi": ["78.44", "68.12", "72.55", "75"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total production = (600 + 628 + 750 + 500 + 570) tonnes = 3048 tonnes</p><p>Total sales = (450 + 525 + 500 + 400 + 516) tonnes = 2391 tonnes</p><p>Required percentage = (2391/3048) * 100 = 78.44%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total production = (600 + 628 + 750 + 500 + 570) tonnes = 3048 tonnes</p><p>Total sales = (450 + 525 + 500 + 400 + 516) tonnes = 2391 tonnes</p><p>Required percentage = (2391/3048) * 100 = 78.44%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The simplified form of the expression [(X<sup>2</sup>  -  1/64) * (1  -  X<sup>2</sup>/64)/(X  -  1/8)(1  -  X/8)] * [1536/(X + 1/8)(1 + X/8)]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; [(X<sup>2</sup> - 1/64) * (1 - X<sup>2</sup>/64)/(X - 1/8)(1 - X/8)] * [1536/(X + 1/8)(1 + X/8)]</p>", "options_en": ["96", "1536", "24", "768"], "options_hi": ["96", "1536", "24", "768"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>[(X<sup>2 </sup> -  1/64) * (1  -  X<sup>2</sup>/64)/(X  -  1/8)(1  -  X/8)] * [1536/(X + 1/8)(1 + X/8)]</p><p>=&gt; 64/ (64 * 64) * [(64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>)/ (8X  -  1)(8  -  X)]/ [1536 * 64/(8X + 1)(8 + X)]</p><p>=&gt; [64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>) * 1536]/ [(64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>)]</p><p>=&gt; 1536 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[(X<sup>2 </sup> -  1/64) * (1  -  X<sup>2</sup>/64)/(X  -  1/8)(1  -  X/8)] * [1536/(X + 1/8)(1 + X/8)]</p><p>=&gt; 64/ (64 * 64) * [(64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>)/ (8X  -  1)(8  -  X)]/ [1536 * 64/(8X + 1)(8 + X)]</p><p>=&gt; [64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>) * 1536]/ [(64X<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(64  -  X<sup>2</sup>)]</p><p>=&gt; 1536 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A rectangular piece of paper is 50 cm long and 22 cm wide. If a cylinder is formed by rolling the paper along its breadth, then the volume of the cylinder is:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332;&#2364; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2369;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; 50 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 22 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332;&#2364; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2342;&#2367;&#2358; &#2328;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2369;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2369;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["2125 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1925 cm<sup>3</sup>", "2025 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1825 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2125 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1925 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "2025 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1825 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Length of rectangular paper = 50cm</p><p>Breadth of rectangular paper=22cm</p><p>After cylinder being formed , </p><p>Breadth of rectangle=circumference of cylinder=22cm</p><p>2*&#960; *R=22</p><p>So R=7/2 cm</p><p>Height=50cm</p><p>Volume= &#960;* R<sup>2</sup>*H=22/7*7/2*7/2*50=1925 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Length of rectangular paper = 50cm</p><p>Breadth of rectangular paper=22cm</p><p>After cylinder being formed , </p><p>Breadth of rectangle=circumference of cylinder=22cm</p><p>2*&#960; *R=22</p><p>So R=7/2 cm</p><p>Height=50cm</p><p>Volume= &#960;* R<sup>2</sup>*H=22/7*7/2*7/2*50=1925 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What value will come in place of question mark (?) in the following question?</p><p>28% of 150 + (?)% of 50  -  36% of 250 = 55% of 80</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361; (?) &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>150 &#2325;&#2366; 28% + 50 &#2325;&#2366; (?)% - 250 &#2325;&#2366; 36% = 80 &#2325;&#2366; 55%</p>", "options_en": ["172", "178", "180", "184"], "options_hi": ["172", "178", "180", "184"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>28% of 150 + (?)% of 50  -  36% of 250 = 55% of 80</p><p>42 + (?) * 0.5  -  90 = 44</p><p><b>? = 184</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>28% of 150 + (?)% of 50  -  36% of 250 = 55% of 80</p><p>42 + (?) * 0.5  -  90 = 44</p><p><b>? = 184</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a + b  -  c = 5 and ab  -  bc  -  ac = 10, then find the value of a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a + b - c = 5 &#2324;&#2352; ab - bc - ac = 10 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["40", "5", "45", "15"], "options_hi": ["40", "5", "45", "15"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Since, (a + b - c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>+ 2ab  -  2bc  -  2ca</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>= (a + b  -  c)<sup>2 </sup> -  2(ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>= 5<sup>2</sup>  -  2 X 10 = 25  -  20 = 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, (a + b - c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>+ 2ab  -  2bc  -  2ca</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>= (a + b  -  c)<sup>2 </sup> -  2(ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2 </sup>= 5<sup>2</sup>  -  2 X 10 = 25  -  20 = 5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two liquids X and Y have the following compositions:</p><p>Liquid X has milk and water in a ratio of 2: 7.</p><p>Liquid Y has milk and water in a ratio of 11: 7.</p><p>If equal quantities of liquids X and Y are used for producing liquid Z, then find the ratio of milk and water in liquid Z.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p>&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Y &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Z &#2340;&#2376;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; Z &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5: 7", "7: 5", "3: 5", "5: 3"], "options_hi": ["5: 7", "7: 5", "3: 5", "5: 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Part of milk in liquid X = 2/9</p><p>Part of milk in liquid Y = 11/18</p><p>Part of water in liquid X = 7/9</p><p>Part of water in liquid Y = 7/18</p><p><img width=159 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image026.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=35 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=27 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image029.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Part of milk in liquid X = 2/9</p><p>Part of milk in liquid Y = 11/18</p><p>Part of water in liquid X = 7/9</p><p>Part of water in liquid Y = 7/18</p><p><img width=159 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image026.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=35 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=27 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23279/image029.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the figure given below, AB II CD and CD II EF. If &#8736;AJI = 129&#730;, &#8736;EFD = 37&#730; and DF II CH, then find the measure of &#8736;GCI.</p><p><img width=271 height=222 id=\"Picture 16\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image013.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB II CD &#2324;&#2352; CD II EF &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;AJI = 129&#730;, &#8736;EFD = 37&#730; &#2324;&#2352; DF II CH &#2361;&#2376;,&#2340;&#2379; &#8736;GCI &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"271\" height=\"222\" id=\"Picture 16\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image013.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["84&#730;", "88&#730;", "86&#730;", "82&#730;"], "options_hi": ["84&#730;", "88&#730;", "86&#730;", "82&#730;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here, &#8736;GCI = &#8736;GCD + &#8736;DCI</p><p>Now, &#8736;DCI = &#8736;BJI = 180  -  129 = 51&#730;</p><p>And, &#8736;GCD = &#8736;EFD = 37&#730;</p><p>Therefore, &#8736;GCI = 51 + 37 = <b>88</b><b>&#730;</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, &#8736;GCI = &#8736;GCD + &#8736;DCI</p><p>Now, &#8736;DCI = &#8736;BJI = 180  -  129 = 51&#730;</p><p>And, &#8736;GCD = &#8736;EFD = 37&#730;</p><p>Therefore, &#8736;GCI = 51 + 37 = <b>88</b><b>&#730;</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person borrowed &#8377;1760 at 6% per annum and &#8377;2240 at 9% per annum at simple interest for the same period. He had to pay &#8377;1536 in all as interest. Find the time (in years).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 6% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 1760 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 9% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 2240 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 1536 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3", "4", "5", "2"], "options_hi": ["3", "4", "5", "2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Interest from &#8377;1760 at 6% = (1760  X  6  X  t)/100 = 105.6t</p><p>Interest from &#8377;2240 at 9% = (2240  X  9  X  t)/100 = 201.6t</p><p>Total interest = 1536</p><p>105.6t + 201.6t = 1536</p><p>307.2t = 1536</p><p>t = 5 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Interest from &#8377;1760 at 6% = (1760  X  6  X  t)/100 = 105.6t</p><p>Interest from &#8377;2240 at 9% = (2240  X  9  X  t)/100 = 201.6t</p><p>Total interest = 1536</p><p>105.6t + 201.6t = 1536</p><p>307.2t = 1536</p><p>t = 5 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B decide to meet a point Y on a particular day from point X. A leaves for point X at 12:00 a.m. at a speed of 36 km/hr. B leaves for point X at 12:30 am the same day A left. At what speed should B travel to catch up with A in 3 hours?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2366;&#2360; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; Y &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2347;&#2376;&#2360;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A 12:00 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; 36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; B &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; 12:30 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; A &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["42 km/hr", "44 km/hr", "46 km/hr", "48 km/hr"], "options_hi": ["42 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "44 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "46 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "48 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Distance covered by A = 36 * 1/2 = 18 km</p><p>In 3 hours, B requires to increase the speed to catchup A by = 18/3 = 6 km/hr</p><p>B's speed = 36 + 6 = 42 km/hr</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance covered by A = 36 * 1/2 = 18 km</p><p>In 3 hours, B requires to increase the speed to catchup A by = 18/3 = 6 km/hr</p><p>B's speed = 36 + 6 = 42 km/hr</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A invest Rs. 20,000 in a business, after 8 months B joined with Rs. 30,000. Find the ratio in which the profit amount should be divided among A and B respectively after a year.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; B &#2344;&#2375; 30,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["2 : 1", "5 : 3", "1 : 1", "3 : 2"], "options_hi": ["2 : 1", "5 : 3", "1 : 1", "3 : 2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio in which the profit amount should be divided between A and B</p><p>=&gt; 20000 * 12 : 30000 * 4 = 24 : 12 = 2 : 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio in which the profit amount should be divided between A and B</p><p>=&gt; 20000 * 12 : 30000 * 4 = 24 : 12 = 2 : 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pooja sells toffees at Rs. 5X per pack, which she purchased for Rs. 50 per pack. However, instead of giving a full 1000 gm pack, she gives only 800 gm while selling. If Pooja's actual profit percentage is 87.5 then find the value of (X + 4)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2370;&#2332;&#2366; 5X &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2335;&#2377;&#2347;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 50 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 800 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2370;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 87.5 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (X + 4) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["19", "15", "21", "27"], "options_hi": ["19", "15", "21", "27"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The ratio of S.P to C.P = (5X/50) * (1000/800) = X/8</p><p>Profit% = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>87.5% = (X  -  8) * 100/8</p><p>700 = (X - 8) * 100</p><p>X = 15</p><p>Now,</p><p>X + 4 = 15 + 4 = 19</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The ratio of S.P to C.P = (5X/50) * (1000/800) = X/8</p><p>Profit% = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>87.5% = (X  -  8) * 100/8</p><p>700 = (X - 8) * 100</p><p>X = 15</p><p>Now,</p><p>X + 4 = 15 + 4 = 19</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;In a triangle KLM, &#8736; M = 90&deg;, if cosec K = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>13", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; KLM &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8736; M = 90&deg; &#2324;&#2352; cosec K =<div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>13", "options_en": ["1/13", "12/13", "25/12", "1/12"], "options_hi": ["1/13", "12/13", "25/12", "1/12"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Cosec K = 13/5 = hypotenuse/perpendicular = KL/LM</p><p>By Pythagoras theorem,</p><p>Base = &radic; (169  -  25) = &radic;144 = 12 = KM</p><p>Now,</p><p>Cos K = base/hypotenuse = KM/KL = 12/13</p><p>Sin L = KM/KL = 12/13</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>[1  -  (12/13)]/ (12/13) = 1/12.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cosec K = 13/5 = hypotenuse/perpendicular = KL/LM</p><p>By Pythagoras theorem,</p><p>Base = &radic; (169  -  25) = &radic;144 = 12 = KM</p><p>Now,</p><p>Cos K = base/hypotenuse = KM/KL = 12/13</p><p>Sin L = KM/KL = 12/13</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>[1  -  (12/13)]/ (12/13) = 1/12.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>At a cafe, Rama bought drinks for her 7 friends at &#8377;240. Some of them wanted coffee, while others wanted black tea. A regular cup of coffee cost &#8377;40 and a regular cup of black tea cost &#8377; 30. How many cups of tea did she purchase?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2376;&#2347;&#2364;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2352;&#2350;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; 7 &#2342;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;240 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2341;&#2368;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2381;&#2354;&#2376;&#2325; &#2335;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2346; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;40 &#2341;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2346; &#2348;&#2381;&#2354;&#2376;&#2325; &#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;30 &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2346; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;?", "options_en": ["5", "4", "3", "6"], "options_hi": ["5", "4", "3", "6"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let x person wanted coffee and 7-x person wanted black tea.</p><p>So x*40+30*(7-x)= 240</p><p>10x=30</p><p>X=3</p><p>So she purchased 7-x=7-3=4 cups.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let x person wanted coffee and 7-x person wanted black tea.</p><p>So x*40+30*(7-x)= 240</p><p>10x=30</p><p>X=3</p><p>So she purchased 7-x=7-3=4 cups.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>KLMN is a parallelogram in which O is point where both diagonals of the parallelogram intersect, such that &#8736;NKM = 37&deg; and &#8736;KOL = 83&deg;. Find &#8736;OLM.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>KLMN &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; O &#2357;&#2361; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#8736;NKM = 37&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;KOL = 83&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;OLM &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["46&deg;", "44&deg;", "36&deg;", "39&deg;"], "options_hi": ["46&deg;", "44&deg;", "36&deg;", "39&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er240611ch6005.png\"></p><p>&#8736;NKM = 37&deg; and &#8736;KOL = 83&deg;.</p><p>&#8736;KML = 37&deg; (By alternate interior angles rule)</p><p>And &#8736;LOM = 180&deg; - &#8736;KOL = 180&deg;  -  83&deg; = 97&deg;</p><p>In &#8710;OML,</p><p>&#8736;OLM = 180&deg; - &#8736;LOM  -  &#8736;OML = 180&deg;  -  97&deg;  -  37&deg; = 46&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er240611ch6005.png\"></p><p>&#8736;NKM = 37&deg; and &#8736;KOL = 83&deg;.</p><p>&#8736;KML = 37&deg; (By alternate interior angles rule)</p><p>And &#8736;LOM = 180&deg; - &#8736;KOL = 180&deg;  -  83&deg; = 97&deg;</p><p>In &#8710;OML,</p><p>&#8736;OLM = 180&deg; - &#8736;LOM  -  &#8736;OML = 180&deg;  -  97&deg;  -  37&deg; = 46&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the following figure, m is a line. If a  -  2b = 30&deg;, then find the measure of (2a+5b)&deg;.</p><p><img width=206 height=111 id=\"Picture 134624456\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21602/image003.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, m &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a - 2b = 30&deg;, &#2340;&#2379; (2a+5b)&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=206 height=111 id=\"&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; 134624456\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21602/image003.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["140&deg;", "130&deg;", "150&deg;", "120&deg;"], "options_hi": ["140&deg;", "130&deg;", "150&deg;", "120&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=206 height=111 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21602/image004.jpg\"></p><p>a  -  2b = 30&deg;</p><p>a = 2b + 30&deg;</p><p>(a + b) + 40&deg; + (7b + 10) = 180&deg;</p><p>2b + 30&deg; + b + 40&deg; + 7b + 10 = 180&deg;</p><p>10b = 100</p><p>b = 10&deg;</p><p>a = 2*10 + 30 = 50&deg;</p><p>2a + 5b = 2*50&deg; + 5*10 = 150&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=206 height=111 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21602/image004.jpg\"></p><p>a  -  2b = 30&deg;</p><p>a = 2b + 30&deg;</p><p>(a + b) + 40&deg; + (7b + 10) = 180&deg;</p><p>2b + 30&deg; + b + 40&deg; + 7b + 10 = 180&deg;</p><p>10b = 100</p><p>b = 10&deg;</p><p>a = 2*10 + 30 = 50&deg;</p><p>2a + 5b = 2*50&deg; + 5*10 = 150&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X + Y = 23 and XY = 112, then what is the value of X<sup>3</sup> + Y<sup>3</sup>? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X + Y = 23 &#2324;&#2352; XY = 112 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>3</sup> + Y<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4430", "3439", "4439", "4450"], "options_hi": ["4430", "3439", "4439", "4450"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>X<sup>3</sup> + Y<sup>3</sup> = (X + Y) (X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= 23 [(X<sup> </sup>+ Y)<sup>2</sup>  -  3XY]</p><p>= 23 (23<sup>2</sup>  -  3 * 112)</p><p>= 23 * 193</p><p>= 4439</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>X<sup>3</sup> + Y<sup>3</sup> = (X + Y) (X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= 23 [(X<sup> </sup>+ Y)<sup>2</sup>  -  3XY]</p><p>= 23 (23<sup>2</sup>  -  3 * 112)</p><p>= 23 * 193</p><p>= 4439</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}]}